    "pdf_page_1based": 721,
    "section": "30.1.7",
    "line_start": 1,
    "line_end": 1,
    "text": "30.1.7 DS Sampler"
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:721:B002",
    "device": "DS Sampler",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "ds-sampler-p721.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 721,
    "section": "30.1.7",
    "line_start": 6,
    "line_end": 6,
    "text": "The DS Sampler Instrument."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:721:B003",
    "device": "DS Sampler",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "ds-sampler-p721.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 721,
    "section": "30.1.7",
    "line_start": 8,
    "line_end": 8,
    "text": "DS Sampler makes use of your own samples to create a drum synth module."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:721:B004",
    "device": "DS Sampler",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "ds-sampler-p721.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 721,
    "section": "30.1.7",
    "line_start": 10,
    "line_end": 11,
    "text": "You can load a sample by dragging and dropping it onto the upper half of the display. The Start control adjusts the position of the sample start, while the Length slider sets the sample playback length."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:721:B005",
    "device": "DS Sampler",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "ds-sampler-p721.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 721,
    "section": "30.1.7",
    "line_start": 13,
    "line_end": 14,
    "text": "You can use the Tune slider to tune your sample by +/- 48 semitones. The Loop switch toggles the sample loop on and off."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:721:B006",
    "device": "DS Sampler",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "ds-sampler-p721.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 721,
    "section": "30.1.7",
    "line_start": 16,
    "line_end": 17,
    "text": "The Decay knob sets the decay time of the sample’s amplitude. The Shaper parameter adds distortion to produce a punchy and gritty sound. The Volume control adjusts the overall level of the instrument."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:731:B001",
    "device": "Expression Control Legacy",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "expression-legacy-p731.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 731,
    "section": "30.3.3",
    "line_start": 16,
    "line_end": 16,
    "text": "30.3.3 Expression Control Legacy"
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:731:B002",
    "device": "Expression Control Legacy",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "expression-legacy-p731.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 731,
    "section": "30.3.3",
    "line_start": 21,
    "line_end": 21,
    "text": "The Expression Control Legacy Effect."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:731:B003",
    "device": "Expression Control Legacy",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "expression-legacy-p731.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 731,
    "section": "30.3.3",
    "line_start": 23,
    "line_end": 25,
    "text": "Expression Control Legacy is a parameter modulation device that allows for a wide variety of internal MIDI mappings. The MIDI controller’s Velocity, Modulation Wheel, Pitch Bend, Aftertouch and Keytrack can each be mapped to one destination."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:731:B004",
    "device": "Expression Control Legacy",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "expression-legacy-p731.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 731,
    "section": "30.3.3",
    "line_start": 27,
    "line_end": 27,
    "text": "Activate a Map switch and click on a parameter in Live to assign that parameter as a mapping target."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:731:B005",
    "device": "Expression Control Legacy",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "expression-legacy-p731.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 731,
    "section": "30.3.3",
    "line_start": 29,
    "line_end": 29,
    "text": "You can set independent modulation intensities for each mapping via the Min and Max sliders."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:731:B006",
    "device": "Expression Control Legacy",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "expression-legacy-p731.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 731,
    "section": "30.3.3",
    "line_start": 31,
    "line_end": 31,
    "text": "The Log and Lin switches toggle between logarithmic and linear shapes."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:731:B007",
    "device": "Expression Control Legacy",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "expression-legacy-p731.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 731,
    "section": "30.3.3",
    "line_start": 33,
    "line_end": 34,
    "text": "The Rise slider smooths the attack of the envelope, while the Fall slider smooths the release of the envelope."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:731:B008",
    "device": "Expression Control Legacy",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "expression-legacy-p731.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 731,
    "section": "30.3.3",
    "line_start": 36,
    "line_end": 36,
    "text": "The Output displays show the output level for each mapping."
  },
  {
    "locator": "MX25:730:B001",
    "device": "Expression Control migration context",
    "source_id": "D12-2025-MAX-GAPS",
    "file": "expression-context-p730.txt",
    "pdf_page_1based": 730,
    "section": "30.3.2",
    "line_start": 1,
    "line_end": 3,
    "text": "The previous version of this device is still available and has been renamed Expression Control Legacy. Live Sets made in Live 11 that contain Expression Control will load the Expression Control Legacy device automatically."
  }
]
